### Page 1 of 3

```text
CITY ATTORNEY’S OFFICE
MUNICIPAL BUILDING
2101 O’NEIL AVENUE, ROOM 308
CHEYENNE, WYOMING 82001
TELEPHONE: (307) 637-6306 | FACSIMILE: (307) 637-6373

MEMORANDUM

To:
 Honorable Mayor Patrick Collins and Members of the City Council

From:
Stefanie Boster, City Attorney

Subject:
Emergency ordinance amending section 10.08.010 of the city code governing the
incorporation of state motor vehicle statutes into city code

Date:
September 23, 2022

Purpose:
The proposed ordinance amends the city code provision governing the enforcement of the City of
Cheyenne's traffic laws. Section 10.08.010 of the city code adopts by reference and incorporates
numerous state statutes under Title 31 of the Wyoming Statutes, which governs motor vehicles.
The incorporated provisions range from vehicle registration, insurance and driver's license
requirements to safety requirements (e.g. seat belt usage and child safety restraints), to the
prohibitions relating to operating a vehicle while under influence. By statute, any city or town that
adopts state statute by reference may only adopt the statutes as they existed at the time of adoption.
Section 10.08.010 currently does not reference a date certain or identify when the code provision
was adopted.

The purpose of the proposed emergency ordinance would be to update the City of Cheyenne's
incorporation (by reference) of these statutory provisions. Adopting the ordinance will avoid
complications and confusion that may arise for the Cheyenne Police Department, the Cheyenne
Prosecutor's Office, and the Municipal Court when determining what specific statutory provision
governs under Section 10.08.010 city code.
```

### Page 2 of 3

```text
ORDINANCE NO. _________

ENTITLED: "AN ORDINANCE AMENDING SECTION 10.08.010, STATE LAW
ADOPTED, OF CHAPTER 10.08, STATE TRAFFIC LAWS ADOPTED, OF
TITLE 10, VEHICLES AND TRAFFIC, OF THE MUNICIPAL CODE OF
THE
CITY
OF
CHEYENNE,
WYOMING,
TO
UPDATE
THE
INCORPORATION OF STATE MOTOR VEHICLE STATUTES."

BE IT ORDAINED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE,
WYOMING:

Section 1.  That Section 10.08.010, State law adopted, of Chapter 10.08, State Traffic Laws
Adopted, of Title 10, Vehicles and Traffic, of the code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, is
hereby amended as set out in this ordinance.

10.08.010 - State law adopted.

The following sections of state law as referenced as in effect on October 1, 2022, but not
including any exclusions enumerated are adopted by reference and incorporated as if fully set out
in this title. A copy of each provision is on file in the office of city clerk.

A. Wyo. Stat. Sections 31-5-101 through and including 31-5-1305 31-5-1402 and Section
31-5-1601, with the exception of Section 31-5-1201, The of the Uniform Act
Regulating Traffic on Highways.

B. Wyo. Stat. Sections 31-7-101 through and including 31-7-138.

C. Wyo. Stat. Sections 31-4-101 through and including 31-4-104, General Offenses and
Penalties.

D. Wyo. Stat. Sections 31-2-201 through and including 31-2-303, The Title and
Registration Act.

E. Wyo. Stat. Sections 31-6-102 through and including 31-6-106, The 31-6-108 of the
Implied Consent to Chemical Testing Act.

F. Wyo. Stat. Sections 31-8-105, the prohibited acts and penalties of The Identification
Card Act.

G. Wyo. Stat. Sections 31-5-1402, requires the use of seat belts in passenger vehicles.

H.G. Wyo. Stat. Sections 31-7-401 through and including 31-7-404, ignition interlock
licenses.

By John Brodie at 2:45 pm, Sep 22, 2022
```

